{"name":"Gumbo","hex":"#718f8a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gumbo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of okra: the plant or its edible capsules.","A soup or stew popular in Louisiana, consisting of a strong stock, meat or shellfish, a thickener (often okra), and the \"Holy Trinity\" of celery, bell peppers, and onions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gumbo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gumbo","blocks":[{"text":"Gumbo is a stew that is popular among the U.S. Gulf Coast community, the New Orleans stew variation being the official state cuisine of the U.S. state of Louisiana. Gumbo consists primarily of a strongly flavored stock, meat or shellfish, a thickener, and the Creole \"holy trinity\": celery, bell peppers, and onions. Gumbo is often categorized by the type of thickener used, whether okra or filé powder. Gumbo can be made with or without okra or filé powder."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Gumbo.JPG/330px-Gumbo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gumbo","wikidata":"Q1160522"},{"title":"Gumbo (PJ Morton album)","blocks":[{"text":"Gumbo is the fourth and first self-released studio album by American singer-songwriter PJ Morton. It was released on April 14, 2017, by Morton Recordings, as the follow-up to his third studio album New Orleans (2013). The record incorporates R&B styles with elements of older soul music; its lyrics discuss themes of romance and explores political and personal themes. The album is entirely produced by Morton himself and features guest appearances by Pell, BJ the Chicago Kid and R&B singer Anthony Hamilton's back-up group, The HamilTones. The album features a cover of the Bee Gees' \"How Deep Is Your Love\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Album_Cover_for_PJ_Morton%27s_CD_Gumbo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gumbo_(PJ_Morton_album)","wikidata":"Q30607194"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Bucket_of_raw_okra_pods.jpg/500px-Bucket_of_raw_okra_pods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Bucket_of_raw_okra_pods.jpg/500px-Bucket_of_raw_okra_pods.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Okra pods","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABucket_of_raw_okra_pods.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Sassafras7.jpg/500px-Sassafras7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Sassafras7.jpg/500px-Sassafras7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sassafras leaves, source of filé powder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASassafras7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Cajun_seafood_gumbo.jpg/500px-Cajun_seafood_gumbo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Cajun_seafood_gumbo.jpg/500px-Cajun_seafood_gumbo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cajun seafood gumbo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACajun_seafood_gumbo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Seafood_Creole_Gumbo.jpg/500px-Seafood_Creole_Gumbo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Seafood_Creole_Gumbo.jpg/500px-Seafood_Creole_Gumbo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Creole seafood gumbo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeafood_Creole_Gumbo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Zherbes.jpg/330px-Zherbes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Zherbes.jpg/330px-Zherbes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gumbo z'herbes, served with filé powder and hot sauce","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZherbes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Gumbo_eatin_%285466684801%29.jpg/500px-Gumbo_eatin_%285466684801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Gumbo_eatin_%285466684801%29.jpg/1280px-Gumbo_eatin_%285466684801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Gumbo_eatin_%285466684801%29.jpg/500px-Gumbo_eatin_%285466684801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A group eating gumbo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGumbo_eatin_(5466684801).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}